[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Welcome to getting started with Quo. In this video, we\'ll walk through how to set up your workspace from scratch. Let\'s jump in. To get started, head over to quo.com and click on start a free trial. Next, you\'ll choose the right plan. Quo offers two primary business plans. The first being business, which'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is great for small teams that need call transferring, AI transcripts and summaries, custom ring orders, and integrations like HubSpot, Jobber, or Salesforce. The scale plan includes everything in business, plus advanced features like AI call tagging. Once'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you\'ve selected a plan, you\'ll create your workspace. If you plan to send SMS messages to US phone numbers, and most people do, you\'ll need to complete an A2P10 DLC registration. I know, a mouthful. In order to register for A2P, you must be'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on a paid account. This is a carrier requirement that helps ensure messages are delivered reliably and remain compliant with US telecom regulations. However, it can take a few days to be approved, so you can continue setting up your workspace while waiting for'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'approval. Now that you have access to your workspace, it\'s time to start inviting team members. To do that, we\'re going to head over to the in app settings. Then click members and invite your team. You\'ll enter each user\'s email to add them to the workspace. If adding multiple users, you can use comma'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'separation between each address. Make sure to assign each of them to a role. They can either be an owner, admin, or member of a workspace. You also have the ability to create a new number for each teammate, or you can add them to one of'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your already existing numbers. We can now move on to routing number setup in the call flow builder. Do you want one central phone number that can be used to ring everyone or will calls need to be routed to different departments with unique call flows? This is something'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that you can figure out with your team. Once phone numbers are assigned to edit a phone number\'s call flow builder, you can navigate to the call flow. This is a drag and drop interface with steps that let you customize exactly how'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'calls should be handled. You can create menu options using a phone menu where you can route calls, add logic prompts, voicemail, fallback logic, or even let AI handle the call. That\'s where Sona, our AI agent, steps in. It can handle'

[01:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'calls automatically, which is great for after hours coverage, lead capture, or as the first point of contact during the day. To add Sona to the call flow, you can drag a Sona step wherever you need it. Sona has many jobs it can handle. It can answer frequently asked questions,'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and it can take messages for leads or call backs. It can communicate location details like addresses, services, or business offerings and anything else you want Sona to be able to answer on your behalf. It can even reply to any SMS communication. And if escalation is'

[02:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'needed and a caller requests to speak with an employee, Sona can transfer calls within your organization. Once you\'ve added Sona and built out the rest of the flow, make sure to test everything. You can test by calling during and after hours, and you can pass through phone menus and listen to how'

[02:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Sona handles sample questions. This ensures your callers have a great call experience from day one. And that\'s it. Following these steps will guarantee a seamless setup with your Quo account and brings you one step closer to being a Quo pro.'
